 I CHOOSE STRATEGY PATTERN - Shipping calculator 
###Pattern Analysis:*
Original has nested if hell: `if shippingMethod == standard/express/overnight` then inside `if country == USA/Canada...` - adding new country or method means editing same function - violates Open/Closed principle. Perfect for Strategy.

*Decomposition Plan:*
- Create Strategy interface: `ShippingStrategy.calculate(package) => cost`
- Concrete strategies: `StandardStrategy`, `ExpressStrategy`, `OvernightStrategy`
- Each strategy owns its country rates + dimensional rules
- Context: `ShippingCalculator` holds map of strategies

*Refactored Code:*
// STRATEGY INTERFACE
class ShippingStrategy {
  calculate(packageDetails, destination) { throw new Error('Must implement'); }
}

// CONCRETE STRATEGIES
class StandardShipping extends ShippingStrategy {
  calculate({weight,length,width,height}, country) {
    let rate = {USA:2.5, Canada:3.5, Mexico:4.0}[country] || 4.5;
    let cost = weight * rate;
    if (weight < 2 && (length*width*height) > 1000) cost += 5.0;
    return cost;
  }
}

class ExpressShipping extends ShippingStrategy {
  calculate({weight,length,width,height}, country) {
    let rate = {USA:4.5, Canada:5.5, Mexico:6.0}[country] || 7.5;
    let cost = weight * rate;
    if ((length*width*height) > 5000) cost += 15.0;
    return cost;
  }
}

class OvernightShipping extends ShippingStrategy {
  calculate({weight}, country) {
    if (country === 'Mexico' ||!['USA','Canada'].includes(country)) {
      return "Overnight shipping not available for this destination";
    }
    let rate = country === 'USA'? 9.5 : 12.5;
    return weight * rate;
  }
}

// CONTEXT + FACTORY
class ShippingCalculator {
  constructor() {
    this.strategies = {
      standard: new StandardShipping(),
      express: new ExpressShipping(),
      overnight: new OvernightShipping()
    };
  }

  calculateShippingCost(packageDetails, destinationCountry, shippingMethod) {
    const strategy = this.strategies[shippingMethod];
    if (!strategy) throw new Error(`Unknown method ${shippingMethod}`);
    const result = strategy.calculate(packageDetails, destinationCountry);
    return typeof result === 'string'? result : result.toFixed(2);
  }

  // Easy to extend - just add new strategy without touching existing code
  addStrategy(name, strategy) {
    this.strategies[name] = strategy;
  }
}

// TESTS - behavior preserved
function runTests() {
  const calc = new ShippingCalculator();
  const pkg = { weight:5, length:10, width:10, height:10 }; // volume 1000

  console.assert(calc.calculateShippingCost(pkg,'USA','standard')==="12.50", "USA standard");
  console.assert(calc.calculateShippingCost(pkg,'Canada','express')==="27.50", "Canada express");
  console.assert(calc.calculateShippingCost(pkg,'USA','overnight')==="47.50", "USA overnight");
  console.assert(calc.calculateShippingCost(pkg,'Mexico','overnight')==="Overnight shipping not available for this destination", "Mexico overnight block");

  // New test for dimensional surcharge
  const smallHeavy = {weight:1, length:20, width:10, height:10}; // volume 2000 >1000
  console.assert(calc.calculateShippingCost(smallHeavy,'USA','standard')==="7.50", "dimensional surcharge 2.5+5");

  console.log("All tests PASS ✅");
}
runTests();

// Usage same as before
const calculator = new ShippingCalculator();
console.log(calculator.calculateShippingCost({weight:5,length:10,width:10,height:10},'USA','standard'));
*Benefits Gained:*

1. *Maintainability:* Before 1 function 45 lines nested. Now 3 classes avg 8 lines each, single responsibility. Fixing Canada rate touches only Standard class, not Express.

2. *Open/Closed:* Want to add `SameDayShipping`? Just `addStrategy('sameDay', new SameDayShipping())` - zero edits to existing strategies. Original required editing giant if-else chain.

3. *Testability:* Can test `new StandardShipping().calculate()` in isolation without passing shippingMethod string.

*Reflection:*

*How did pattern improve maintainability?*
Removed conditional complexity from 3 levels to 1 lookup. Each shipping rule now isolated - junior dev can't accidentally break express when fixing standard.

*What future changes easier?*
- Add new country: just edit rate map in that strategy, not all methods
- Add new shipping method: new class, no regression risk
- Add promo/discount decorator: can wrap strategies
- Change dimensional rules per method: contained

*Unexpected challenges?*
Had to decide where to put `toFixed(2)` - should stay in context not strategies, so strategies return numbers (except error message). Also error handling: overnight not available - return string vs throw - kept string to preserve original behavior but better would throw custom error.

